# 12 — Feature Rules: Per-Feature Implementation Guide

## How to Use This File
Before implementing any feature, find its section below and read it fully.
These rules prevent common mistakes and ensure $0 cost, security, and good UX.

---

## 📝 Blog

**Architecture**: Static Generation — markdown files in `src/content/blog/`

### Rules
- All blog posts are `.md` or `.mdx` files — NO database for blog content
- Frontmatter schema defined in `src/content/config.ts` (typed)
- `draft: true` posts excluded from build (`getCollection` filter)
- Slug = filename (Astro handles automatically)
- Images: local images in `src/assets/blog/` → Astro optimizes to WebP
- No paid CMS — content is in the GitHub repo
- Reading time: calculate at build time from word count (no package needed)

### SEO Checklist (per post)
- [ ] Unique `title` (max 60 chars) in frontmatter
- [ ] `description` (max 160 chars) in frontmatter
- [ ] `ogImage` specified or default used
- [ ] Heading hierarchy: one `<h1>` (title), then `<h2>` and below in content

### Cost: $0 — Static files, no DB calls

---

## 📔 Notes

**Architecture**: Two types — Public notes (SSG, content collection) + Private notes (SSR, Supabase DB)

### Public Notes
- Same pattern as blog — `.md` files in `src/content/notes/`
- No auth required to view

### Private Notes
```typescript
// Supabase table: notes
// Columns: id, user_id, title, content (text), is_public, created_at, updated_at
// RLS: user_id = auth.uid() for all operations
```
- Private notes require Google login
- Editor: simple `<textarea>` — no rich text library needed initially
- Auto-save: debounced `UPDATE` to Supabase (500ms debounce — reduces API calls)
- Content stored as plain text/markdown — no HTML in DB (prevents XSS)

### Cost: $0 — within Supabase 500MB free tier (text is tiny)

