## 🎮 Browser Games

**Architecture**: Client-side only — pure HTML5 Canvas / vanilla JS

### Rules
- Games run 100% in browser — NO server calls during gameplay
- Use Astro `client:only="vanilla"` island or plain `<script>` tags
- Canvas-based games: no external game engines — keep bundle small
- Scores are saved to Supabase ONLY after game over (one DB call per session)
- Guest play allowed — scores only saved if user is logged in
- Each game lives in its own directory: `src/components/games/[game-name]/`

```typescript
// Game score save pattern (client-side, after game over)
async function saveScore(gameSlug: string, finalScore: number) {
  const session = await supabase.auth.getSession();
  if (!session.data.session) return; // Not logged in — silently skip

  await supabase
    .from('game_scores')
    .insert({ game_slug: gameSlug, score: finalScore });
    // RLS sets user_id = auth.uid() automatically
}
```

### Leaderboard
- Public leaderboard: top 10 scores per game
- Query: `SELECT score, profiles.username FROM game_scores JOIN profiles ... ORDER BY score DESC LIMIT 10`
- Cache leaderboard for 60 seconds in component state — don't re-fetch on every render

### Cost: $0 — games are static assets, DB calls are minimal

