## 👤 User Profiles

**Architecture**: SSR — requires auth session

### Supabase Table
```sql
CREATE TABLE profiles (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  username TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  display_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  avatar_url TEXT,
  bio TEXT,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

ALTER TABLE profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Users can read any profile" ON profiles FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own profile" ON profiles FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = id);
```

### Rules
- Profile auto-created on first Google login (Supabase Auth trigger or app-level)
- Avatar: upload to Supabase Storage `avatars/` bucket — max 200KB, WebP format
- Public profiles: anyone can view (username, display_name, bio, avatar)
- Private fields: none currently (keep it simple)
- Username: alphanumeric + underscore only — validate with regex before insert

### Cost: $0 — minimal DB, avatar in Storage (1GB free limit)

