## 🔖 Bookmarks & Progress

**Architecture**: SSR — requires auth session

### Supabase Tables
```sql
-- Bookmarks
CREATE TABLE bookmarks (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  url TEXT NOT NULL,
  title TEXT NOT NULL,
  notes TEXT,
  tags TEXT[] DEFAULT '{}',
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE bookmarks ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Own bookmarks only" ON bookmarks USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Reading progress (for blog posts)
CREATE TABLE reading_progress (
  user_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  post_slug TEXT NOT NULL,
  progress_pct INTEGER DEFAULT 0,  -- 0-100
  completed BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  PRIMARY KEY (user_id, post_slug)
);
ALTER TABLE reading_progress ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Own progress only" ON reading_progress USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

### Rules
- Save reading progress: debounced (every 10% scroll or on page leave) — reduce DB calls
- Bookmarks: simple list view — no folder hierarchy initially (YAGNI)
- Tags: stored as text array in Postgres — no separate tags table

### Cost: $0 — minimal rows, well within 500MB

